      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 1116,
        "height": 1228,
        "content": "\ud83d\udcd8 WORKFLOW DETAILS\n\n# Biopharma Cold-Chain Lot Release & Excursion CAPA Router\nTurns IoT excursion evidence into a defensible release, quarantine, or destroy recommendation.\n\nFor: biopharma QA and distribution teams\nProblem: temperature excursions are assessed inconsistently and evidence is scattered\n\nExecution path\n1. Receive Excursion Telemetry\n2. Normalise Lot Evidence\n3. Fetch Stability Envelope\n4. Extract Excursion Facts\n5. Provide Extraction Model\n6. Compute Thermal Debt Score\n7. Check Immediate Quarantine\n8. Create Quality Case\n9. Wait for QA Evidence Window\n10. Draft Disposition Rationale\n11. Provide Drafting Model\n12. Check Destroy Threshold\n13. Archive Excursion Evidence\n14. Log Disposition Audit\n15. Alert Quality Leadership\n16. Email Release Package\n\nNode summary\n- Receive Excursion Telemetry: trigger step.\n- Normalise Lot Evidence: transform step.\n- Fetch Stability Envelope: transform step.\n- Extract Excursion Facts: ai step.\n- Provide Extraction Model: ai step.\n- Compute Thermal Debt Score: transform step.\n- Check Immediate Quarantine: branch step.\n- Create Quality Case: storage step.\n- Wait for QA Evidence Window: branch step.\n- Draft Disposition Rationale: ai step.\n- Provide Drafting Model: ai step.\n- Check Destroy Threshold: branch step.\n- Archive Excursion Evidence: storage step.\n- Log Disposition Audit: storage step.\n- Alert Quality Leadership: notify step.\n- Email Release Package: notify step.\n\nInput: sensor webhook with lot, lane, stability limits and time-series readings\nOutput: quality case, evidence archive, disposition draft and alerts\n\nColour legend: trigger=1, transform=2, AI=3, branch=4, storage=5, notify=6."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "580696cb-d91f-4fa3-9af2-2fed331623c3",
      "name": "Master Panel 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1184,
        656
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 700,
        "height": 388,
        "content": "\u2699\ufe0f SETUP GUIDE\n\n1. Import this JSON via n8n \u2192 Workflows \u2192 Import from File.\n2. Create/select credentials: OpenAI Reasoning account; Operations API Header Auth; Gmail Operations account; Google Sheets Compliance account; Google Drive Evidence account; Telegram Operations bot, where used.\n3. Replace all REPLACE_WITH_* values, example.com URLs, recipients, sheet/folder IDs, chat IDs and policy thresholds.\n4. Pin a realistic test payload at the trigger and run manually.\n5. Confirm branch, stored record and notification before activation.\n\nEstimated setup: 25\u201345 minutes.\nDifferentiator: Uses cumulative thermal debt plus stability-envelope evidence, not a generic temperature threshold alert."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "581885f3-9a43-408f-83cb-fa79a6e0215c",
      "name": "Master Panel 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1168,
        1088
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 668,
        "height": 228,
        "content": "\ud83c\udfa8 CUSTOMISATION\n\n- Edit policy Code nodes to match local thresholds.\n- Replace the final notification node with Slack, Teams or PagerDuty.\n- Add a human approval branch before irreversible external actions.\n- Add a second sink after the audit merge for BI reporting.\n- Adapt the same evidence model to an adjacent regulated process."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "cdcc0cfa-715d-4121-be90-93c9ae80cfce",
      "name": "Master Panel 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1168,
        1376
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 652,
        "height": 372,
        "content": "\u2139\ufe0f ADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\nExternal calls continue on regular output and retry 3 times with a 2-second delay. Failed calls remain visible for audit handling. AI and vendor API cost scales with record count; add batching for high volume. Minimise personal or regulated data sent to models and apply retention controls to stored evidence. Built to current stable conventions as of 2026-09-29; exact node versions use the supplied fallback and should be confirmed on first local import. No live n8n instance was available. Known limitation: placeholder endpoints and credentials must be replaced.\n\nCreator: Swapnil AI Labs \u2014 swapnil.mandloi7@gmail.com \u2014 swapnilailabs.netlify.app"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
